== 58A.1  a miss costs 19 times a false alarm
t* = c_FP/(c_FP + c_FN) = 1/20 = 0.0500
log-odds threshold ln(c_FP/c_FN) = ln(1/19) = -2.9444   (check: logit(t*) = -2.9444)
p = 0.04: say yes costs (1-p)*c_FP = 0.96, say no costs p*c_FN = 0.76 -> no ; p < t*
p = 0.06: say yes costs (1-p)*c_FP = 0.94, say no costs p*c_FN = 1.14 -> yes ; p >= t*
p = 0.0500: yes 0.9500  no 0.9500
p = 0.0499: yes 0.9501  no 0.9481
p = 0.0501: yes 0.9499  no 0.9519
at p = t* both actions cost 0.9500

== 58A.2  8 rows, 3 positive truths, 5 predicted positive, accuracy 6/8
n1 = 3, n0 = 5, m1 = 5, m0 = 3  baseline accuracy = 0.7500
expected accuracy after a shuffle (Eq. 58.4-2) = (3*5 + 5*3)/64 = 30/64 = 0.46875
importance I = 0.7500 - 0.46875 = 0.28125
average over all 8! = 40320 orders: 0.46875
distribution of the accuracy after a shuffle: {0.0: 720, 0.25: 10800, 0.5: 21600, 0.75: 7200}
share of orders with accuracy at least the baseline 0.75: 0.1786
P(prediction agrees with truth) for a positive truth: m1/n = 5/8; for a negative truth: m0/n = 3/8
sum over rows: 3*(5/8) + 5*(3/8) = 3.750  ->  divided by n: 0.46875
